2026-05-09 17:35:10,713 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:35:10,713 - INFO - **The scale argument**: The observable universe contains an estimated 2 trillion galaxies, each with hundreds of billions of stars. Many of those stars have planets. The sheer statistical improbability that Earth is the *only* place where life emerged—across this incomprehensibly vast space—is hard to defend.
