2026-05-09 17:49:10,014 - INFO - **My actual view:**
2026-05-09 17:49:10,015 - INFO - The tradeoff is real and contextual. Some speech restrictions can improve outcomes; others make things worse. The question isn't "freedom or restriction?" but "which specific restrictions, in which contexts, with what safeguards?" That requires case-by-case analysis, not principled absolutes in either direction.
