2026-05-09 17:50:21,408 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:50:21,408 - INFO - 1. **"Excessively medicalized"** — Modern psychiatry *does* treat serious conditions (bipolar disorder, schizophrenia, severe depression with suicide risk) where medication demonstrably saves lives. The question isn't whether to medicalize at all, but where to draw lines.
2026-05-09 17:50:21,408 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:50:21,408 - INFO - 2. **"Pathologizing normal emotions"** — Clinical depression isn't sadness; clinical anxiety disorder isn't worry. These have specific criteria that distinguish them from normal responses. The problem is fuzzy boundary cases, not fundamental confusion about what's normal.
